# Project development rules

Read `DEVELOPMENT_RULES.md` and `AGENTS.md` before architectural changes.

## Stack

React + Vite + TypeScript · NestJS + TypeScript · MariaDB + Prisma · Redis · BullMQ

## Must

- TypeScript strict; avoid `any`
- Thin controllers; business logic in services; DI
- Provider interfaces for all external services
- Document every env var in `.env.example`
- Never hard-code credentials or expose secrets to React
- MariaDB only — never PostgreSQL
- Schema changes only via Prisma migrations
- Transactions for financial/critical ops
- Validate every API request; auth ≠ authorization
- Tenant-isolate customer data; rate-limit; audit sensitive admin actions
- Never log passwords, tokens, or API secrets

## AI tools

Every tool: authN, authZ, validation, tenant check, rate limit where needed, audit.

AI must NOT auto: delete accounts/hosting/DBs, change prod DNS, refund, deploy prod, modify billing, change permissions — human approval required.

## Feature workflow

Inspect → read docs → plan → DB/API/security impact → implement → tests → lint → typecheck → test → build → fix → report. Never ignore failing tests.
